I would suggest following -

ret = ioctl(fd, I2C_SLAVE_FORCE, device_address);
if (ret < 0)
{
   this->close();
   return ret;
}


You are already in error path, so failing a close fd is also fine, as long as you return an error to the caller that the  full-open(open+ioctl) operation has failed.

With your current code it will return success in this error path as fd close will succeed most probably (as it was just opened).

